            <ArticleTitle>[Peculiarities and complexities of questioning the patient in myocardial infarct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author depicted several cases of myocardial infarction which onset or preinfarction angina symptoms were taken by the patients for a catarrhal disease. The signs enabling the doctor to exclude the &quot;catarrhal&quot; origin of patient's feelings were indicated. The author suggested that the term of &quot;catarrhal&quot; variant of myocardial infarction onset&quot; should be used as a pattern of its atypical onset.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
